# Nordveil is free (Milestone 25b; Cory: a victory scene for every freed
# kingdom). Plays in the town the first time you arrive after the Frozen
# Sovereign falls (Town._play_victory), right after the color washes back
# across the Tundra; KingdomVictory's short movie card follows. {a1}-{a3} are
# the other three heroes; the party walks up from the gate into the square
# while the townsfolk pour out of their houses.

spawn {a1} {a1} at 15,19 facing up
spawn {a2} {a2} at 17,19 facing up
spawn {a3} {a3} at 16,19 facing up
music town
move player to 16,12 async
move {a1} to 15,13 async
move {a2} to 17,13 async
move {a3} to 16,14 async
spawn kid1 child at 5,15 facing up
spawn neighbor1 worker at 24,15 facing up
spawn neighbor2 merchant at 6,4 facing down
move kid1 to 12,12 async
move neighbor1 to 20,12 async
move neighbor2 to 13,10 async
sync
face player up
emote kid1 heart
emote neighbor1 note
say Captain: Do you feel it? The wind's gone warm. The blizzard is over - truly over.
say Captain: The Frozen Sovereign held Nordveil by the throat for months. You walked into his citadel and broke his grip.
emote player note
say Elder: The shrine's flame caught on the very first spark. Nordveil has not seen a morning like this in a generation.
say Child: Mama! Mama, the snow is sparkly again!
emote frank note
say Frank: Ha! Look at all these faces. That's what a kingdom looks like when it can breathe again.
say Frank: Two more to go. Duskara burns in the west, and Selavon drowns to the east. But tonight? Tonight, Nordveil lights its fires for you.
say Captain: Nordveil's gates are yours, now and always. Rest, eat, and let the forge outfit you. You've earned it.
